      "body": "A compressed-tensors FP8_DYNAMIC MoE checkpoint (per-tensor weight scale, per-token dynamic activations) could not reach the native XPU MoE backend and failed with \"Unsupported FP8 MoE backend: NONE\". Two selection gates blocked it; both are fixed here (neither is sufficient alone):\r\n\r\n1. XPUExpertsFp8._supports_quant_scheme: accept (kFp8StaticTensorSym, kFp8DynamicTokenSym). XpuFusedMoe takes unquantized activations and quantizes them inside the kernel, so per-token dynamic activation scaling is equivalent for its purposes.\r\n\r\n2. CompressedTensorsW8A8Fp8MoEMethod.__init__: allow the (TENSOR weight, TOKEN activation) strategy combination (previously it fell through to an assert requiring BLOCK).\r\n\r\nScope: enables per-tensor-weight FP8 checkpoints on the native XPU MoE. Does not address per-channel weights, which still route to the Triton FP8 MoE fallback.\r\n\r\nValidated serving DiffusionGemma-26B-A4B-it FP8 on 4x Intel Arc Pro B70; the log selects \"Using XPU Fp8 MoE backend\" and output is coherent.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\n\r\n---\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Essential Elements of an Effective PR Description Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [ ] The purpose of the PR, such as \"Fix some issue (link existing issues this PR will resolve)\".\r\n- [ ] The test plan, such as providing test command.\r\n- [ ] The test results, such as pasting the results comparison before and after, or e2e results\r\n- [ ] (Optional) The necessary documentation update, such as updating `supported_models.md` and `examples` for a new model.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n",
